      "guid": "com.crocodilejonesy.configraidstatus",
      "name": "Configurable End Raid Status",
      "slug": "configurable-end-raid-status",
      "teaser": "A simple mod that allows you to change the raid exit statuses to something else (e.g MIA to survived)",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2657.png",
      "downloads": 2182,
      "favourites_count": 2,
      "description": "<p>Hate it when the raid ends with 1 second left to extract?</p>\n<p>Sick and tired of having to commit fully to a raid when something comes up?</p>\n<p>Look no further, this mod has got you covered.</p>\n<p>This is a simple mod that allows you to set whatever raid status you desire for each of the raid statuses in-game;</p>\n<p>You can set MIA will to survived (so you extract even when the timer runs out).</p>\n<p>You can make it out safely even when your character falls over from a grenade.</p>\n<p>Or you can even set survived status to left the action if you like to live on the edge</p>\n<p>The choices are yours.</p>\n<p>For the ‘survived’ option, there is a toggle to enable/disable it just incase.</p>\n<p>Installation is simple;</p>\n<p>Just open the zip and drag and drop the bepinex folder into your spt install</p>\n",
